{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/42798-goblin-chronicles-stopgap-gmc-changes-for-changeling","id":42798,"title":"Goblin Chronicles(?): Stopgap GMC changes for Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-05T03:49:47-08:00","id":42798,"title":"Goblin Chronicles(?): Stopgap GMC changes for Changeling","content":"While any Chronicles update of <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Changeling: The Lost </b></span>will probably have some more significant overhauls (like I'm sure a predatory aura-like fae mien), there are at least a few simple things we can do in the meantime. I'll go through the core book here and, with B&amp;S, GMC and <b>Demon </b>in mind as far as mechanical changes, come up with a few suggestions. These won't be as extensive as a full treatment probably receives, but it's something.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Character Creation</b></span><br /> Changelings get 10 Merits at character creation. They may spend 5 Merit dots to increase starting Wyrd by one dot.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Merits</b></span><br /> With the exception of Supernatural Merits as usual, changelings can purchase Merits out of the GMC book. As per the book, Social Merits might require some explanation, but use common sense and Storyteller discretion.<br /> <br /> <b>Hollow</b><br /> Similar to the Bolthole Merit from <b>Demon: The Descent</b>, Hollow now<br /> <br /> <b>Mantle</b><br /> See below.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Contracts</b></span><br /> <b>Smoke 4: Murkblur</b><br /> Success inflicts the Blinded Tilt for the duration (see<b> God-Machine Chronicle</b>, p. 208).<br /> <br /> <b>Artifice 3: Blessing of Perfection</b><br /> If the object so blessed is a weapon, its bonus is equal to the changeling's Wyrd divided by 2 (rounding down). The character divides these bonus points as she wishes between the weapon's Damage and Initiative ratings.<br /> <br /> <b>Darkness 1: Creeping Dread</b><br /> Success inflicts the Scarred Condition on all affected targets.<br /> <b>Darkness 2: Balm of Unwakeable Slumber</b><br /> This causes both the Insensate and Immobile Tilts as the target suffers from a magically-enforced sleep. Both Tilts immediately end if the target is harmed in any way or endangered (truly vigorous shaking or slapping a sleeping target also work), but otherwise the target remains asleep until she is accustomed to waking up. On an exceptional success, the target is Drugged for the rest of the scene after waking up.<br /> <br /> <b>Elements 1: Cloak of the Elements</b><br /> Ignore any damage from the relevant extreme environment while the clause is active.<br /> <b>Elements 2: Armor of the Elements' Fury</b><br /> The armor provided is 1/1. It downgrades one level of firearms damage to bashing, and subtracts 1 point from overall damage. As with weapon changes, the elemental Wyrd damage applies as a Damage bonus after a successful attack roll. It no longer applies to the attack roll itself.<br /> <b>Elements 5: Become the Primal Foundation</b><br /> Armor gained by transforming into a solid element has a general rating equal to Wyrd, and a ballistic rating equal to half the character's Wyrd, rounded down. The damage provided by a damaging element once again applies after a successful attack roll, as if delivered by a weapon with Damage rating equal to half the character's Wyrd.<br /> <br /> <b>Fang and Talon 1: Tongues of Birds and Words of Wolves</b><br /> An exceptional success puts the Bonded Condition on the animal.<br /> <b>Fang and Talon 3: Pipes of the Beastcaller</b><br /> Exceptional success grants the Bonded Condition along with the other effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Stone 5: Red Rage of Terrible Revenge</b><br /> Armor gained is 1/1.<br /> <br /> <b>Vainglory 1: Mask of Superiority</b><br /> Maybe adds the Swooned Condition?<br /> <b>Vainglory 4: Mantle of Terrible Beauty</b><br /> Those who roll fewer successes than the changeling suffer from the Frightened and Humbled Conditions. On an exceptional success, even those who roll more successes are Humbled in the character's presence. This is in addition to the changeling's bonus to Intimidate rolls.<br /> <b>Vainglory 5: Words of Memories Never Lived</b><br /> Success puts the False Memories Condition on listeners. On an exceptional success, the targets are all Mesmerized for the duration as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Fleeting Spring 5: Waking the Inner Faerie</b><br /> Inflicts the Obsession Condition on the target.<br /> <br /> <b>Eternal Summer 1: Son of the Hearth</b><br /> This power negates the penalties for extreme environments of heat or cold in the affected area (determined by the user as normal). Also renders targets immune to Extreme Heat and Extreme Cold Tilts.<br /> <b>Eternal Summer 5: The Lord's Dread Gaze</b><br /> The attack roll is Dexterity + Athletics - target's Defense. If successful, apply a Damage modifier equal to the changeling's Mantle divided by two (round up).<br /> <br /> <b>Fleeting Autumn 2: Tale of the Baba Yaga</b><br /> This applies the Frightened Condition to targets.<br /> <b>Fleeting Autumn 5: Mien of the Baba Yaga</b><br /> Also applies the Frightened Condition to targets.<br /> <br /> <b>Fleeting Winter 3: Faces in the Water</b><br /> Applies the Broken Condition to the target for the duration (and others suffer the -2 penalty to influence the subject).<br /> <b>Fleeting Winter 4: Fallow Fields, Empty Harvest</b><br /> Inflicts the Joyless Condition (see below).<br /> <b>Fleeting Winter 5: Every Sorrow a Jewel</b><br /> Causes the Insensate Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Eternal Winter 1: Jack's Breath</b><br /> Creates a level 2 or 3 extreme environment (cold), depending on the degree to which the room is cooled.<br /> <b>Eternal Winter 3: Riding the Devil's Jawbone</b><br /> Applies the Extreme Cold Environmental Tilt on the affected area, which doesn't affect the changeling herself.<br /> <b>Eternal Winter 4: Fallen from the Timbers</b><br /> The roll is Dexterity + Athletics - the subject's Defense. Success adds half the character's Wyrd (rounded up) to the damage, which is lethal. Subject still suffers other penalties.<br /> <b>Eternal Winter 5: Witch's Paradise</b><br /> Creates a level 2 extreme environment over a wide area by default. Each additional five successes does one of the following: increase the level by 1, double the radius, increase duration by 1 hour.<br /> <br /> <b>Goblin: Diviner's Madness</b><br /> After divining, you suffer from the Madness Condition for one day.<br /> <br /> <b>New Condition: Joyless</b><br /> Your character can no longer feel positive emotions, only coldness and crushing negativity. With no capacity for joy or happiness, you become unable to regain Willpower by acting on Virtues or Vices (or their equivalent) and suffer a -2 penalty to all Social rolls.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Possible Sources: </b>Dramatic failure on a detachment roll, Fleeting Winter clause<b>s</b><br /> <b>Resolution: </b>The character experiences an overwhelmingly joyous new experience (the birth of a child, the profession of deep-seated love by someone)</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Special Rules and Systems</b></span><br /> Nothing really changes by default. However, I am not much of a fan of Mantle as it stands being a Merit. Honestly, since it seems like most supernaturals will have a sort of predatory aura equivalent, I think Mantle should be folded into fae mien in the changeling version of a predatory aura. Not sure how to compensate for its inclusion in seasonal Contracts, since using Wyrd all the time wouldn't necessarily fit (and could get much more powerful with Wyrd 6+). Yet half Wyrd is too low, I think. However, I don't think Mantle is really something you should pay for on its own. If you include it in the &quot;aura,&quot; its effects are felt on some level even by mortals, but just covered by the Mask.<br /> <br /> It's late, I'm tired, I will consider it more tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T04:19:00-08:00","id":42805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/42798-goblin-chronicles-stopgap-gmc-changes-for-changeling#post42798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Hollow</b><br /> Similar to the Bolthole Merit from <b>Demon: The Descent</b>, Hollow now</div> </div> </div> </div>This sentence is unfinished.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/42798-goblin-chronicles-stopgap-gmc-changes-for-changeling#post42798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing really changes by default. However, I am not much of a fan of Mantle as it stands being a Merit. Honestly, since it seems like most supernaturals will have a sort of predatory aura equivalent, I think Mantle should be folded into fae mien in the changeling version of a predatory aura. Not sure how to compensate for its inclusion in seasonal Contracts, since using Wyrd all the time wouldn't necessarily fit (and could get much more powerful with Wyrd 6+). Yet half Wyrd is too low, I think. However, I don't think Mantle is really something you should pay for on its own. If you include it in the &quot;aura,&quot; its effects are felt on some level even by mortals, but just covered by the Mask.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would rather keep Mantle as it is and let it apply a small bonuses to certain uses of the aura effect in addition to the current Mantle style of bonuses.<br /> <br /> As for what the aura does, I'd say that Changelings have a natural ability to inflict any emotion they want; with a tinge that it's so pure it hurts. In a good way. With a very good roll a changeling could inflict Fear so terrible you're paralysed, but a part of you likes that feeling. It's like a roller coaster, despite the fact you'd have to be mad to do anything that scary (like jumping off a cliff, fear exists for a good reason).<br /> <br /> This tinge of madness is the equivilent of the vampire's predatory nature. Vampire's only create unhealthy predatory feelings. Changeling's care create healthy emotions, but they tend to overdo it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-05-2014, 07:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T04:54:26-08:00","id":42813,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'm not sure Changelings actually need a predatory aura equivalent outside of the need to be able to clash...and even then outside of Bedlam, it doesn't really feel appropriate.<br /> <br /> Mantle is mostly fine, if a bit messy I would say. Mantle is basically a supercharged supernatural status with perks. They power some of the most potent contracts, give significant social bonuses and they all come with some nice abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T08:27:49-08:00","id":42892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/42798-goblin-chronicles-stopgap-gmc-changes-for-changeling#post42798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Stone 5: Red Rage of Terrible Revenge</b><br /> Armor gained is 1/1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even with the new changes to armour, that frankly sounds a little on the low side for a five-dot power which earlier could provide an uncapped amount of protection. (Unless of course it still meant 1/1 per success.)<br /> <br /> Oddbody's option for the equivalent of chainmail could probably be just handled by the new armour chart?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">(Previously known by the name of &quot;GrimGent&quot;.)</span>","edited":{"userid":335,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/335-the-yann-waters","user":"The Yann Waters","date":". 01-05-2014, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/335-the-yann-waters","name":"The Yann Waters","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T12:13:27-08:00","id":43056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Yann Waters</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/42798-goblin-chronicles-stopgap-gmc-changes-for-changeling?p=42892#post42892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with the new changes to armour, that frankly sounds a little on the low side for a five-dot power which earlier could provide an uncapped amount of protection. (Unless of course it still meant 1/1 per success.)<br /> <br /> Oddbody's option for the equivalent of chainmail could probably be just handled by the new armour chart?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, wow, I totally missed that it was 1 point of armor per success. 1/1 per success might be a bit much. I might do 1 general armor per success and 1 ballistic every two successes. So, 4 successes gets you 4/2 armor (very potent, indeed), while 2 still gets you 2/1.<br /> <br /> Changlings don't necessarily need a predatory aura in the sense of cowing people with their supernatural might (outside of Vainglory, of course), but I think extending fae mien into an aura-like effect would be good. Mantle's effects just seem to me like something that should be linked to Wyrd or whatnot automatically; having to pay for them seems unfair to me. However, Mantle also does power some Contracts, so yeah, it's not an easy solution.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of all the big supernaturals at least having some kind of aura-like effect. For vampires and werewolves it might be a sense of danger and hunger, predatory. For changelings, it would be a tinge of fae madness, glimpses of other worlds hidden just beyond sight and things like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T15:35:08-08:00","id":43171,"title":"","content":"I'd simply (or not so simply) wrap Bedlam into their Aura. Get too big a dose of the weirdness they project (and hide via the Mask), and things start to get unhinged. It's something I'm working on, given my long-term game with my Co-ST has Changeling and Werewolf antagonists; I don't see a good reason to short change them, and I always felt Bedlam along with Hedge-sculpting had too high of base Wyrd requirements.<br /> <br /> I want to give them 3 permutations for each Attribute + Wyrd used; they may use Finesse rather than Power though just to present some differences. I'm thinking a form of Bedlam for the Social or physical (emotions/impulses running unchecked), Madness for the mental or social(though I'm not entirely sure I want to use the Madness Condition) as individuals start to see portions of Faerie and the Wyrd bleed over onto things like a low-Clarity Changeling, and... something for the physical. Or, switch it up some, have one that occludes clear memories, a nod to The Mask where you lash out with it's supernaturally obscuring properties, likely a Mental attribute base. <br /> <br /> Honestly, I've little problem with Mantle as is beyond filling in the 2 and 4 dot benefits. One -could- work Mantle into the Aura but nothing is clicking that doesn't seem a stretch or unnecessarily penalizing to those without a Court. Perhaps a minor bonus to the Bedlam Condition for emotions in line with the court as part of the Mantle benefit package? <br /> <br /> Still all very rough stuff mind you, I'm not satisfied with a proper division yet and what where yet, but it's starting to gel. Madness, Emotions Unbridled, Obscured Memory; all have some touches within the Changelings themselves, so it -could- work but I'm still brain storming. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T16:34:45-08:00","id":43206,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't remove the Mantle Merit, is it should be possible for someone with a high Wyrd to have a low Mantle and the other way around. Your Mantle is your connection to the Court (and season) and has nothing to do with your connection to the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Mantle currently is a combination of Status within a court and a magical aura (with some other benefits). Someone with a high Mantle cannot necessarily boss his court around, but is still respected. The other way around high Mantle is required for some Court positions. You could make an argument for differentiating between the magical connection with your Court and Status within your Court, where having a high Mantle could make it easier to gain Status. What position you have within your Court would then be a function of both Status and Mantle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T17:15:53-08:00","id":43233,"title":"","content":"I feel as though it might be neat to see Mantle integrated as a substitute for Wyrd as the Court Contracts seem to hint at it being \u2014 maybe adjusting Glamour rate and capacity to [higher of (Mantle+1) and (normal Wyrd-based rate)] and [higher of (Mantle+10) and (normal Wyrd-based capacity)], respectively, so that a Wyrd 1, Mantle 5 changeling and a Wyrd 6 changeling are distinguished by the more evident things and there's a bit more of an inbuilt inequity between the Courts and the Courtless that pushes the Courtless to be more likely to raise Wyrd and the makes Courts more likely to view the Courtless as potential Fae catspaws.<br /> <br /> It's an idle thought.<br /> <br /> (Tying Mantle to bedlam/aura mechanics would also be neat, probably.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T06:45:29-08:00","id":44134,"title":"","content":"An idea that hit me in the shower earlier for Mantle mechanics: Make them work like the Agenda conditions for Demon: The Descent.<br /> <br /> For those that aren't familiar: DtD allows you to choose an agenda, which gives you a condition that you can resolve for a bonus and meet a condition for a beat that lasts once per session. Each court has three divergent, but appropriate focuses (mostly, but I'm thinking we should keep it simple): The Signature Emotion, The Season/Direction/Time of Day and the Agenda (War, Espionage, Occultism, Rebirth). As such, pick one of the three for your character with the mantle and it gives you the condition helpful in aiding their cause.<br /> <br /> An example for Summer (this is very rough): There's no reason that you couldn't apply these conditions to your contracts of the court either.<br /> <br /> Enraging<br /> Beat: Encourage or convince someone to anger when they wouldn't have otherwise.<br /> Resolution: Expend this condition to gain a Bonus of Mantle Dots on any test related to anger.<br /> <br /> Heat of the Sun<br /> Beat: Endure or create an environment where you suffer from a harsh or bright environment.<br /> Resolution: Expend this condition to gain a Bonus of Mantle Dots on any test to create heat, light or fire.<br /> <br /> Noon Light Knight<br /> Beat: Initiate a contest or battle when diplomacy, stealth or other means would have sufficed.<br /> Resolution: Expend this condition to gain a bonus of Mantle Dots on an action in the first round of Combat.<br /> <br /> The social bonus for same-court should probably help set impression levels if you want to use the Doors system. Likewise it should help inflicting bedlam of your chosen emotion.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Concerns? Mathematical alterations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T08:42:29-08:00","id":44190,"title":"","content":"As a side note, I think the Contract of the Moon is going to need to be altered quite heavily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T10:19:12-08:00","id":44969,"title":"","content":"While we're on the subject of Goblin Chronicles. I propse that Changelings be given a buff to The Mask: Use the Demon Spoofing rules, but with a dicepool of 11-Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Though Unlike Demons' spoofing there's pretty reliable (Ensorcellment, being a Fae) ways to outright bypass The Mask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T12:41:19-08:00","id":45065,"title":"","content":"I've read on here about people modifying Integrity to make it into a new Clarity mechanic that's more to their liking. Would anyone like to share specifics of how that's done?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T13:22:28-08:00","id":45090,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/9736-the-innocence-system-from-the-walking-shadows-campaign-integrity-et-al-replacement\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...al-replacement</a> Check the third post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T18:33:56-08:00","id":45275,"title":"","content":"Another interesting thing I noted from the Hunter Blog Post recently (<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-the-vigil-the-faithful-of-shulpae/\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a>).<br /> <br /> Apparently attributes are governed by the Sanctity of Merits rule - this has a pretty significant impact on Goblin Contracts that sacrifice attribute dots to use. Willpower is at least codified to have to be rebought if it's lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T21:20:43-08:00","id":45371,"title":"","content":"Goblin Contracts of Sacrifice could readily use Persistent Conditions as their cost rather than Dot spending however, with heavy duty Resolutions to get rid of them as an alternative to mucking around in that too much. Some could still costs a Willpower Dot (or more?) but I think this might be an area where the Condition set could supplant the prior costs. Resolutions in of themselves give a whole lot of cool stuff one can put in to make them evocative, as well as Beats vs just Attribute/Willpower loss as the cost.<br /> <br /> Much the same with the Fan-made Contract of the Moon and Sun dealing with the emotive aspects (something of which I had to do my own rewrite and tinker of some time ago); if Changelings aren't using Virtue and Vice and instead use something like Claire's mention some time back with Mask and Seeming on the old forums, (or was it Mask and Mien?) it may just be easier to pop down Conditions for the appropriate levels that penalize certain actions and/or encourage others along with other factors. Honestly, I think they'd work better under that model regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T23:20:37-08:00","id":45411,"title":"","content":"Goblin Contracts in general could (and probably should with an official rules revision) be re-written to give a negative condition on your character rather than eating dots of willpower/attributes or whatnot. What with all the other Goblin Contracts essentially giving you negative conditions and the like as it is. It's also why I'm a fan of the 1XP a Dot for Goblin Contracts - the power itself isn't the cost, but what it costs to use them in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T15:10:57-08:00","id":45868,"title":"","content":"Given I have to do some updates for the C:tL portion of a game I co-run ASAP anyhow, here's a semi-crazy thought:<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of rolling Bedlam into their &quot;Aura&quot; as stated before, the heavy wave of emotion/madness they can let out (without it being tied to a specific Wyrd Tier to gain access to). But what if, as one of the 3 effects (I want some symmetry cross-splat) one is ensorcellment as a Condition, if not Fae-Touched as another term for it? Cut out the necessity of Pledges to create the effect (at least in the short term, instead in the long term) as a way for a Changeling to reveal themselves to a mortal or other, a temporary glimpse past the Mask? Toss in some other effects into the Condition, and I think this may work quite well instead of blowing through all your Glamour like the old base mechanic (something I house-ruled some time back anyhow).<br /> <br /> The third? I'm looking at something similar in basic concept to the old Locked effect from DA: Fae. Instead presenting the Changeling's distancing, regression, or denial of their Fae aspects while the Fae-Touched or whatever a better name for the Condition is used reflects a strong focus/embrace of it. The third would create a sort of plausible deniability effect within the scope of a Condition's potency; you're more likely to deny, rationalize or not notice the weirdness around you; for mortals it'd be a way of reinforcing the Mask against specific individuals, as well as other supernatural. When reflected back on the Changeling, it'd reflect a retreat into their human side.<br /> <br /> All 3 would be wrapped also into Imbalance (or whatever you would name Clarity loss; perhaps some synonym for Lost would be best evocative) to reflect the fae side, the human side, and the unbridled mad side of being between/part of both for Clarity loss, with some other effect (Broken? Something else?) condition wise for a Dramatic failure.<br /> <br /> I'm going to tinker with this model some for their Aura; obviously it sucks to suffer from as the Changeling, but I want it to have a beneficial edge to inflict on others. Also, I'd like it to reinforce that Changeling Courts and social interactions can be rather mad, unpredictable affairs, and as a supernatural outsider, dealing wtih them is fairly precarious to your sanity too. Being 'ensorceled' against your will would be anything but pleasant when Faerie starts to bleed into your reactions and perceptions of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T16:59:43-08:00","id":45915,"title":"","content":"Interesting changes there. But those aside, I think I'd honestly like it if Mantle remained as a merit, because as it's been stated, the Mantle is a Changeling's personal connection to the Court they're aligned to and is also a mixture of several social factors concerning it.<br /> <br /> Now, what I'd really like is getting the Mantle 1 benefit for the Autumn Court fixed. Well, I say fixed, but the text in the corebook is probably an error or something. Because &quot;two bonus dice on any Contract activation roll that uses Occult&quot; is a little stupid and very underwhelming compared to the other mantles when there is only a single <i>Clause </i>of a single Contract in the corebook that even uses Occult.<br /> <br /> I always assumed it meant &quot;2 bonus dice on any Contract activation roll&quot;. Because it would make sense. &lt;,&lt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-06-2014, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}